{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "האלה ואמרו רק עם", :translit "ha'eleh ve'ameru rak am", :gloss "these and they said only a nation"} {:he "מקוה", :translit "mikveh", :gloss "ritual bath"} {:he "ערוה", :translit "ervah", :gloss "nakedness"} {:he "למה ערות אחותו אסורה וערות בת אחיו מותרת", :translit "lammah ervot achoto asurah ve'ervot bat achiv muteret", :gloss "why is the nakedness of his sister forbidden yet the nakedness of his brother's daughter permitted"} {:he "למה מקוה מ' סאה מטהר ואם חסר קורטוב אינו מטהר", :translit "lammah mikveh mem se'ah metaher ve'im chaser kortov eino metaher", :gloss "why does a mikveh of forty se'ah purify and if a kortov is lacking it does not purify"} {:he "רק מיעוטא הוא שאינם יודעים טעם כלאים ופרה וכיוצא בהם", :translit "rak mi'uta hu she'einam yod'im ta'am kil'ayim u'parah u'cheyotzeh bahem", :gloss "it is only a diminution that they do not know the reason for kil'ayim and the red heifer and similar things"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "האלה ואמרו רק עם", :spells "מקוה"} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "רק עם", :spells "ערוה"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'only a wise and understanding people' (Deuteronomy 4:6) is understood midrashically to mean that Israel's reputation for wisdom rests not on mastering the reasons for the commandments but on faithfully observing them. The red heifer is the classical example of a decree whose rationale eludes human understanding: Rabban Yohanan ben Zakkai declared to a non-Jew that it purifies the impure by divine decree, not by any natural explanation (Yoma 67a; Pesikta Rabbati 14). Laws such as forbidden relations and the forty-se'ah minimum of the mikveh are treated as gezerot whose exact thresholds and categories are fixed by decree, not deducible from reason (Yoma 67a). The word 'רק' functions as a limitation: their wisdom is that they observe even what they cannot rationally explain.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 4:6" "Yoma 67a" "Pesikta Rabbati 14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "האלה ואמרו רק עם", :spells "מקוה", :letters ["ה" "ו" "ק" "ם"], :by :selah, :order :bag} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "רק עם", :spells "ערוה", :letters ["ר" "ע"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:57.351415917Z", :model "glm-5.2"}